From 7489cf0b1603e5148c90f71ca61e2d4cecb67c5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 18:37:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 03/94] cpufreq: qcom-hw: only read a DCVS control register
 that exists

Per-core DCVS is probed by reading reg_dcvs_ctrl, but that offset is
zero on OSM revisions that have no such register, so the driver reads
whatever lives at the start of the frequency domain region and can
conclude from an unrelated bit that per-core DCVS is available.  It then
writes a performance state request per CPU, at reg_perf_state plus four
bytes per core, into registers that are something else entirely.

Only probe the register when the SoC data says there is one.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/cpufreq/qcom-cpufreq-hw.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/cpufreq/qcom-cpufreq-hw.c b/drivers/cpufreq/qcom-cpufreq-hw.c
index d2ddb73ad..2a503309f 100644
--- a/drivers/cpufreq/qcom-cpufreq-hw.c
+++ b/drivers/cpufreq/qcom-cpufreq-hw.c
@@ -1654,7 +1654,9 @@ static int qcom_cpufreq_hw_cpu_init(struct cpufreq_policy *policy)
 		return -ENODEV;
 	}
 
-	if (readl_relaxed(data->base + qcom_cpufreq.soc_data->reg_dcvs_ctrl) & 0x1)
+	/* Offset zero is not a DCVS control register on every OSM revision */
+	if (qcom_cpufreq.soc_data->reg_dcvs_ctrl &&
+	    readl_relaxed(data->base + qcom_cpufreq.soc_data->reg_dcvs_ctrl) & 0x1)
 		data->per_core_dcvs = true;
 
 	ret = qcom_cpufreq_hw_read_lut(cpu_dev, policy);
